1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,156
For half a century,

2
00:00:01,156 --> 00:00:04,867
every graduation speech and job interview revolved around one

3
00:00:04,867 --> 00:00:06,205
intimidating question:

4
00:00:06,205 --> 00:00:08,639
where do you see yourself in five years?

5
00:00:08,639 --> 00:00:11,681
That question made sense in nineteen seventy-five,

6
00:00:11,681 --> 00:00:14,905
when corporate career ladders moved at glacial speed.

7
00:00:14,905 --> 00:00:18,616
In an AI-accelerated economy where tools and entire workflows

8
00:00:18,616 --> 00:00:20,563
transform every eighteen months,

9
00:00:20,563 --> 00:00:24,092
locking yourself into a rigid five-year script creates two

10
00:00:24,092 --> 00:00:25,430
painful failure modes:

11
00:00:25,430 --> 00:00:28,046
endless analysis paralysis before starting,

12
00:00:28,046 --> 00:00:31,575
or sunk-cost misery climbing a ladder you secretly outgrew

13
00:00:31,575 --> 00:00:32,183
years ago.

14
00:00:32,183 --> 00:00:33,948
In her book Tiny Experiments,

15
00:00:33,948 --> 00:00:38,145
neuroscientist Anne-Laure Le Cunff replaces linear life planning with

16
00:00:38,145 --> 00:00:40,457
a far more adaptable operating system:

17
00:00:40,457 --> 00:00:42,830
treating your career like a laboratory.

18
00:00:42,830 --> 00:00:46,939
Traditional goals fail because they anchor your self-worth to

19
00:00:46,939 --> 00:00:49,431
outcomes you cannot directly control,

20
00:00:49,431 --> 00:00:53,204
like hitting ten thousand subscribers or landing a dream

21
00:00:53,204 --> 00:00:54,281
title by thirty.

22
00:00:54,281 --> 00:00:56,033
When progress starts slow,

23
00:00:56,033 --> 00:00:58,188
perfectionism tells you to quit.

24
00:00:58,188 --> 00:01:02,028
Le Cunff flips this script with a simple scientific Pact:

25
00:01:02,028 --> 00:01:05,059
I will perform one specific action at a clear

26
00:01:05,059 --> 00:01:06,406
cadence for a short,

27
00:01:06,406 --> 00:01:10,179
bounded duration - such as publishing one visual insight

28
00:01:10,179 --> 00:01:12,334
every morning for fourteen days,

29
00:01:12,334 --> 00:01:16,106
or building three small automation scripts in two weeks.

30
00:01:16,106 --> 00:01:17,925
During those fourteen days,

31
00:01:17,925 --> 00:01:20,417
you ignore vanity metrics completely.

32
00:01:20,417 --> 00:01:22,236
Success is binary and calm:

33
00:01:22,236 --> 00:01:25,200
did you show up and collect real-world data?

34
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:28,897
Tiny Experiments become even more powerful when paired with

35
00:01:28,897 --> 00:01:32,344
systems theorist John Gall's nineteen seventy-five law:

36
00:01:32,344 --> 00:01:35,665
every complex system that works evolved from a simple

37
00:01:35,665 --> 00:01:37,232
system that worked first.

38
00:01:37,232 --> 00:01:41,869
Ambitious beginners routinely spend six months in private designing logos,

39
00:01:41,869 --> 00:01:42,809
legal entities,

40
00:01:42,809 --> 00:01:46,318
and forty-page curricula for an audience they have never

41
00:01:46,318 --> 00:01:48,512
tested - only to launch to silence.

42
00:01:48,512 --> 00:01:52,460
A fourteen-day experimental pact forces Version One simplicity.

43
00:01:52,460 --> 00:01:54,277
By shipping ten short essays,

44
00:01:54,277 --> 00:01:55,843
five prototype templates,

45
00:01:55,843 --> 00:01:59,541
or three concise video breakdowns in public over two weeks,

46
00:01:59,541 --> 00:02:03,050
you collect honest market signal for zero dollars before

47
00:02:03,050 --> 00:02:04,930
investing months of your life.

48
00:02:04,930 --> 00:02:08,138
Look closely at almost any category-of-one creator,

49
00:02:08,138 --> 00:02:08,642
founder,

50
00:02:08,642 --> 00:02:11,913
or independent analyst and you will notice a secret:

51
00:02:11,913 --> 00:02:15,185
almost none of them predicted their winning niche on

52
00:02:15,185 --> 00:02:15,688
day one.

53
00:02:15,688 --> 00:02:16,191
Instead,

54
00:02:16,191 --> 00:02:19,777
they ran four or five consecutive tiny experiments across

55
00:02:19,777 --> 00:02:20,847
a single quarter.

56
00:02:20,847 --> 00:02:23,111
Loop one tested productivity habits;

57
00:02:23,111 --> 00:02:25,376
loop two tested visual storytelling;

58
00:02:25,376 --> 00:02:29,654
loop three combined behavioral economics with automated dashboards -

59
00:02:29,654 --> 00:02:33,051
and suddenly one specific angle sparked five times the

60
00:02:33,051 --> 00:02:36,889
reader replies while feeling like effortless play to produce.

61
00:02:36,889 --> 00:02:40,223
You cannot think your way into unfair career leverage

62
00:02:40,223 --> 00:02:41,230
on a whiteboard;

63
00:02:41,230 --> 00:02:44,690
you uncover it through low-stakes contact with reality.

64
00:02:44,690 --> 00:02:46,941
When a fourteen-day pact finishes,

65
00:02:46,941 --> 00:02:49,987
how you review the data determines everything.

66
00:02:49,987 --> 00:02:53,298
Amateurs treat small early numbers as a verdict on

67
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:54,159
their talent.

68
00:02:54,159 --> 00:02:57,403
Scientists open a single notebook page and run Le

69
00:02:57,403 --> 00:03:00,648
Cunff's ten-minute Plus-Minus-Next retrospective.

70
00:03:00,648 --> 00:03:01,376
Under Plus,

71
00:03:01,376 --> 00:03:05,150
list what gave you energy and resonated with real people.

72
00:03:05,150 --> 00:03:05,945
Under Minus,

73
00:03:05,945 --> 00:03:09,719
note the exact bottlenecks that felt unnecessarily heavy.

74
00:03:09,719 --> 00:03:10,447
Under Next,

75
00:03:10,447 --> 00:03:13,625
choose one of three calm paths for the following

76
00:03:13,625 --> 00:03:14,288
two weeks:

77
00:03:14,288 --> 00:03:16,406
Persist if momentum is building,

78
00:03:16,406 --> 00:03:19,254
Pivot one variable such as format or topic,

79
00:03:19,254 --> 00:03:23,690
or consciously Pause the experiment guilt-free with lessons banked.

80
00:03:23,690 --> 00:03:26,905
Retire the pressure of figuring out the next five

81
00:03:26,905 --> 00:03:30,907
years and design one fourteen-day Tiny Experiment today using

82
00:03:30,907 --> 00:03:31,694
three rules.

83
00:03:31,694 --> 00:03:32,285
Rule one:

84
00:03:32,285 --> 00:03:35,697
write a single concrete pact sentence - for example,

85
00:03:35,697 --> 00:03:39,830
I will publish one three-hundred-word mental model breakdown or

86
00:03:39,830 --> 00:03:43,504
build one useful spreadsheet template every two days for

87
00:03:43,504 --> 00:03:44,423
fourteen days.

88
00:03:44,423 --> 00:03:45,013
Rule two:

89
00:03:45,013 --> 00:03:48,622
cap daily execution under forty-five minutes so you can

90
00:03:48,622 --> 00:03:51,574
complete every rep alongside a full-time job.

91
00:03:51,574 --> 00:03:52,296
Rule three:

92
00:03:52,296 --> 00:03:55,642
refuse to judge metrics until day fourteen arrives,

93
00:03:55,642 --> 00:03:58,069
then run your Plus-Minus-Next review.

94
00:03:58,069 --> 00:03:59,644
Six tiny loops from now,

95
00:03:59,644 --> 00:04:02,990
your skills and direction will look unrecognizable.
